class.description:
[LoadProgress] is the one progress model for loading several files: [signal ResourceDatabase.preload_progress] and [method ResourceDatabase.get_preload_progress] report the files of [method ResourceDatabase.preload_from] (a [Preloads], also with [FilesManifest]s), [method ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get_manifest_status] reports a [FilesManifest] that is loaded directly, and [method TransitionScreen.get_load_progress] reports a scene transition. The same code shows any of them, for example "3 / 12 loaded" and a progress bar:
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _process(_delta):
    var progress := ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get_manifest_status(manifest)
    $Label.text = "%d / %d loaded" % [progress.get_loaded_count(), progress.get_total_count()]
    $ProgressBar.ratio = progress.get_ratio()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Process(double delta)
{
    LoadProgress progress = ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGetManifestStatus(manifest);
    GetNode<Label>("Label").Text = $"{progress.GetLoadedCount()} / {progress.GetTotalCount()} loaded";
    GetNode<ProgressBar>("ProgressBar").Ratio = progress.GetRatio();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
A snapshot does not change after it was created: ask again (or wait for the next signal) for newer values.
